# pref-enum.aon --- the disjunct spelling of "allowed set with a
# default". FIXED 2026-08-26 by the preference admission gate
# (ADR-004): an override must be admitted by an alternative (or equal
# the preferred value), so v:"9.9" is now REFUSED under vet
# ([aontu/empty], verdict invalid) where it used to vet VALID --
# this file was kept as evidence of that gap. The pref_not_instance
# advisory still accompanies the schema (the default "1.0" is not an
# instance of any remaining alternative -- write *"1.0"|"1.0"|"1.1"
# to state it as a first-class member and silence it). The conjunct
# spelling used by envelope.aon, ("1.0" | "1.1") & *"1.0", enforces
# under vet but still errors under plain eval and loses the default in
# canon (probes/default-a.aon / default-b.aon -- the phase-1 limit).

E: v: *"1.0" | "1.1"
